invariant: INV-48
file: keccak_avx2.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh mlkem-avx2
reason: the start writes each state's second index first, so state k
  absorbs seed || x1[k] || x0[k], the stream of the transposed
  entry. Only an x86-64 compiler reads the line, so the script builds
  bin/mlkem_avx2_equiv_test for x86-64 and runs it under
  qemu-x86_64. The lane skips without docker, and this then reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
        s->lane[4][k] = (uint64_t)x0[k] | ((uint64_t)x1[k] << 8) | ((uint64_t)0x1f << 16);
--- new
        s->lane[4][k] = (uint64_t)x1[k] | ((uint64_t)x0[k] << 8) | ((uint64_t)0x1f << 16);
